1. Direct Answers: Did OMG Really Help, How, and By How Much?
Did OMG really improve November performance despite the low start? Yes.
The Low Starting Baseline: In September (pre-OMG), network Smiley was stuck at 75.56% (dipping as low as 74.27% in WB Sept 13). When OMG first launched on Oct 2, live coaching was low (19.4%–21.2% of audits), OMG QA dipped to 73.04%, and network Smiley hit an October low of 75.36% in WB Oct 11 (74.05% on Oct 13; Manila Core averaged 73.87% for October). Even November 1 opened low at 76.36%.
The Inflection & Climb: Once OMG shifted on Oct 16–19 from passive grading to real-time floor coaching, live interventions more than doubled (19.4% in WB Oct 11 → 30.7% in WB Oct 18 → 49.6% in WB Oct 25 → 45.7%–49.3% in early Nov). Network Smiley rose every full week after that—climbing from 75.36% (WB Oct 11) → 76.68% → 77.01% → 78.22% → 79.53% → 80.02% in WB Nov 15 (79.27% Nov MTD, +2.96 points vs. Oct and +3.71 points vs. Sept).
How did OMG directly drive that lift?
Stopped bad fixes before the survey went out: Live interventions rose from 28.5% to 40.6% of SBS audits (1,972 → 2,144 chats), cutting Wrong Resolutions by 81% (3.25% untouched vs. 0.61% intervened).
Turned bottom-quartile agents around: Tracking the same 176 October bottom-quartile agents (Oct QA under 65%) into November, their OMG QA jumped +15.2 points (48.8% → 64.0%) and their in-chat resolution climbed +10.0 points (41.1% → 51.1%).
Contained repeat DSAT outliers: Auditing 33%–40% of all network non-smileys each week cut raw DSATs from October's top 236 outliers by -56.8% (3,685 → 1,591 cases), shrinking their share of floor DSATs from 55.8% to 37.9%.
What is the Direct Impact of OMG Only (Stripping Out Trainings & Product Fixes)?
Network-Wide Direct OMG Impact: Because every site inside the same LOB received the same global Billing & Payments ("Money") Training, MV Macro, and product updates, comparing high-OMG sites against low/zero-OMG peer sites within the exact same LOB isolates pure OMG floor impact at ~+0.47 to +0.55 points of the +2.96-point total November gain (~270–315 extra Smileys across 57,153 Nov surveys, or ~16%–19% of the entire company lift—and +1.06 to +1.44 points inside high-adoption sites). The remaining ~+2.4 points came from shared trainings, self-serve macros, and product fixes.
Core (75.25% → 78.26% | +3.02 points total gain): Low-OMG peer sites set a +2.48-point non-OMG baseline (India/MTQ at 4.9% live coaching gained +2.37 points; Cali/ARN at 4.1% live coaching gained +2.54 points). High-OMG Manila/PHX (69.3% live coaching) jumped +3.92 points (+1.44 points above baseline) and Clark/HTW (57.8% live coaching) rose +2.85 points (+0.37 points above baseline), proving a +0.57-point direct OMG-only lift across Core (~19% of Core's total gain, or ~222 extra Smileys).
Plus (81.72% → 83.53% | +1.81 points total gain): Low-OMG Manila/PHX (11.7% live coaching; 8.4 interventions per 1k tickets) gained +1.25 points, while high-OMG Clark/HTW (40.4% live coaching; 25.2 interventions per 1k tickets) jumped +2.31 points (+1.06 points above Manila)—delivering a +0.54-point direct OMG-only lift across Plus (~30% of Plus's total gain, or ~20 extra Smileys).
Premium (77.95% → 80.81% | +2.86 points total gain): Zero-intervention Cali/ARN (0.0% Nov live coaching) gained +2.68 points, whereas high-OMG Clark/HTW (80.0% live coaching; 92% QA) climbed +3.19 points (+0.51 points above baseline) and Manila/PHX (60.0% live coaching) rose +2.81 points (+0.13 points above baseline), adding +0.20 points of direct OMG-only lift across Premium (~7% cross-site lift, alongside outlier PIP containment).
Retail (79.92% → 83.33% | +3.41 points total gain): Operating in a single site (Manila/PHX), Retail logged just 0.49% live coaching (1 chat, or ~0.00 points of live-intervention lift), as the POS v11.16.0 patch and Hardware training drove +2.7 points of the gain; however, OMG's 91.0% DSAT scrub coverage (81 of 89 non-smileys reviewed) guided the remaining +0.7-point non-POS improvement.
